  "details": "The Video Player is not working in any world regardless of what I do. The error is always the same, shortly, \"unable to load video\", but also usually \"Loading failed. File not found, codec not supported, video resolution too high or insufficient system resources.\" I've tried disabling firewalls, using VPNs, disabling vsync, clearing any and all data, reinstalling, replacing the yt-dlp a few different ways, bypassing with cookies, and a few other things I've seen. It didn't work with Meta Link, or Steam VR. My internet is fast and it worked when I had wayyy worse internet. The only thing it works on now for me personally is my standalone Quest 2. Attatched are what should be my earliest report before trying any solutions, as well as after I tried all of them.",
